He had just worked in prisons and he designed this completely new facility. I understand that there was some interesting architectural features of this facility, Pelican Bay. The cement for the facility was poured in one large block, and so that the cells were not built in individual units? Mm-hmm. So, one of the things that's striking about the places it's made of these poured concrete cells, so they're incredibly easy to hose down, which is the fact that they can stay clean is important because quartz earlier had criticized isolation units for being
他只是在监狱工作过，就设计了这个全新的设施。据我了解，这个设施——鹈鹕湾监狱——有一些有趣的建筑特点。该设施的水泥是一大块浇筑的，所以牢房不是建在单个的单元里的？嗯哼。所以，关于这个地方引人注目的一点是，它是用这些浇筑的混凝土牢房组成的，所以它们极其容易用水管冲洗保持清洁，这一点很重要，因为科茨早些时候曾批评隔离区——

