if you can imagine that structure. I'm wondering, Kermad, if you can actually just describe what one of these cells looks like. Give me a sense of what's in the cell, how big it is. What does it actually feel like to be in one of these units? So the cells in these units are generally about 8 by 10 feet. So imagine a wheelchair accessible bathroom stall or a generous parking space. Pretty small. You can almost reach from one end of the cell to the other. And they're fairly self-contained. So they contain a poured concrete ledge with a very thin piece of foam over it, and that's
如果你能想象那种结构的话。卡拉米特，我想知道你是否能具体描述一下其中一个牢房是什么样子的。让我对牢房里的东西以及它有多大有个概念。身处其中一个单元究竟是什么感觉？这些单元里的牢房通常大约是8乘10英尺。所以想象一下无障碍卫生间的隔间，或者一个宽敞的停车位。相当小。你几乎可以从牢房的一端够到另一端。而且它们相当自给自足。所以它们包含一个浇筑的混凝土矮台，上面铺着一张非常薄的海绵垫，那就是——

